# Courier – Out for Delivery (OFD) UI Rule

## Objective
Implement the full courier Out-for-Delivery (OFD) flow UI using Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind, and shadcn/ui. UI-only with mocked data; no API calls. Follow `@naming-and-scoping.mdc` for IDs and class naming.

## Tech & Sources
- Stack: Next.js 14+, TypeScript, Tailwind, shadcn/ui components already in repo (`Button`, `Card`, `Badge`, `Tabs`, `Input`, `Textarea`, `Avatar`, `Alert`).
- Dialog/Modal: use shadcn/ui Dialog pattern (Context7 guidance: accessible Dialog). Toasts may use existing lightweight banners or Sonner-like pattern; prefer the existing in-repo toast style.
- Animations: transform/opacity only, 200–250ms, respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Accessibility: keyboard support, ARIA roles, focus-visible. No keyboard traps.

## Files to Add
- `app/courier/out-for-delivery/page.tsx` (main page)
- Optional composables under `app/courier/out-for-delivery/`:
  - `StopsList.tsx` – list of assigned stops
  - `CurrentStopCard.tsx` – details of selected stop
  - `AttemptDialogs.tsx` – delivered/failed modal UIs

## Mock Data Model (local constants)
```
type StopStatus = "pending" | "en_route" | "delivered" | "failed";
type Stop = {
  id: string;            // unique
  sequence: number;      // 1..N
  name: string;          // recipient
  address: string;
  eta: string;           // e.g., "14:10–14:30"
  status: StopStatus;
  phone?: string;
  notes?: string;
};
```

## Page Layout
- Header (`parcego-ofd-header`)
  - Back ghost icon button `parcego-ofd-back-btn` (`ArrowLeft`), routes to `/courier`.
  - Title: “Out for Delivery”.
  - Status `Badge` (In Progress/Paused) `parcego-ofd-status-badge`.

- Summary Card (`parcego-ofd-summary-card`)
  - Stats: total, remaining, delivered count, simple progress bar.
  - Actions: `Pause`/`Resume`, `Refresh` (UI only) with subtle transitions.

- Main Content (responsive)
  - Desktop ≥lg: 12-col grid → Stops list (lg:col-span-5) + Current stop (lg:col-span-7).
  - Mobile: Column stack; sticky action bar persists.

- Stops List (`parcego-ofd-stops-list`)
  - Each stop row: sequence chip, recipient, address, ETA, status badge.
  - Row CTA icons: `Navigation` (deeplink placeholder), `Phone`, `MessageSquare`, `Scan`.
  - Selection: click/Enter toggles current stop; selected row has border+bg emphasis and `aria-pressed=true`.

- Current Stop Card (`parcego-ofd-current-card`)
  - Recipient, phone, delivery notes, small map placeholder (Card with `MapPin`).
  - Primary CTAs: `Attempt Delivery` (opens dialog), `Pre-drop Scan` (opens scan dialog).

- Attempt Delivery Dialog (`parcego-ofd-attempt-dialog`)
  - Tabs or segmented control: Delivered | Failed.
  - Delivered: photo placeholder, optional “Require signature” checkbox; Confirm button `parcego-ofd-delivered-confirm-btn` → sets status `delivered`, toast success, auto-advance to next pending.
  - Failed: reason radios (No answer, Incorrect address, Access blocked, Other), optional notes + photo placeholder; Confirm button `parcego-ofd-failed-confirm-btn` → sets status `failed`, toast warning; remains on stop.

- Sticky Action Bar (`parcego-ofd-stickybar`)
  - Left: “Stop X of N • Remaining Y”.
  - Right: `Navigate`, `Call`, `Attempt Delivery` (primary). Sticks bottom on mobile; edge-shadow.

- Offline Banner (`parcego-ofd-offline-banner`)
  - Appears at top when `isOffline=true`. Text about queued actions; `Retry` button (UI only).

## Status Badges (Tailwind color tokens)
- delivered: `bg-green-100 text-green-800 border-green-200`
- failed: `bg-red-100 text-red-800 border-red-200`
- en_route: `bg-blue-100 text-blue-800 border-blue-200`
- pending: `bg-gray-100 text-gray-800 border-gray-200`

## IDs & Naming (must be unique)
- Prefix all IDs with `parcego-` and describe component/purpose: e.g., `parcego-ofd-stop-item-{id}`, `parcego-ofd-attempt-dialog`, `parcego-ofd-scan-dialog`.
- Follow `@naming-and-scoping.mdc` for uniqueness and clarity.

## Interactions (UI-only state)
- Selecting a stop sets `selectedStopId` and highlights row.
- Attempt Delivery dialog controls mutate local `stops` state only.
- “Resume/Pause/Refresh” affect labels and show a toast; no network.
- Navigation/Call/Message actions are placeholders; do not leave app.
- Progress bar recalculates on any status change.

## Accessibility
- List rows are buttons: `role="button"`, `tabIndex=0`, keyboard activate on Enter/Space.
- Dialogs: `role="dialog" aria-modal="true"`, focus sent to first actionable element; escape and overlay close.
- Toasts/banners: `aria-live="polite"`.
- Ensure sufficient color contrast and focus-visible rings.

## Responsive Rules
- Mobile: list stacks under current card, sticky bar always visible.
- Tablet: two columns; reduce gaps; CTA text truncates with `min-w-0`/`truncate`.
- Desktop: grid split 5/7; hover states add subtle shadow + `scale-[.98]` on active.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Summary, list, current card render with mocked data; no API.
- Delivered/Failed flows update status badges immediately and adjust progress.
- Pre-drop scan dialog opens and shows mock success on submit.
- Sticky action bar works at all sizes; offline banner toggles via flag.
- All IDs follow `parcego-...` and are unique.
- No layout shift; only transform/opacity animations.

## Build Notes
- Reuse existing `Icon` names in repo (`MapPin`, `Navigation`, `Phone`, `MessageSquare`, `ScanBarcode`, `CheckCircle`, `AlertCircle`).
- Keep components small and pure; no dead code or TODOs.
- Do not import external SDKs (maps, camera). Use placeholders.

## Implementation Checklist
1) Create page at `app/courier/out-for-delivery/page.tsx` with header, summary, grid shell.
2) Add mocked `stops: Stop[]` and derive counts/progress via memo.
3) Implement `StopsList` with selectable rows and status badges.
4) Implement `CurrentStopCard` with CTAs and map placeholder.
5) Implement `AttemptDialogs` with Delivered/Failed tabs and confirm actions.
6) Add sticky bar and offline banner; ensure a11y on dialogs/controls.
7) Verify IDs, responsiveness, reduced-motion, and keyboard paths.

# Courier – Out for Delivery (OFD) UI Rule

## Objective
Deliver a clean, responsive, and fully navigable UI for the courier “Out for Delivery” flow using shadcn/ui, Tailwind, and the project’s naming-and-scoping rules. UI only; all data mocked.

## Tech & Conventions
- Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind, shadcn/ui.
- Components: `Button`, `Card`, `Badge`, `Tabs`, `Input`, `Textarea`, `Avatar`, `Alert` (as available in repo).
- IDs must follow project pattern with `parcego-` prefix, unique and descriptive. See `@naming-and-scoping.mdc`.
- Transitions: subtle only (opacity/transform), respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Accessibility: keyboard, roles, aria, focus-visible; no keyboard traps.

## Files
- Add: `app/courier/out-for-delivery/page.tsx`
- Optional shared UI:
  - `app/courier/out-for-delivery/StopsList.tsx`
  - `app/courier/out-for-delivery/CurrentStopCard.tsx`
  - `app/courier/out-for-delivery/AttemptDialogs.tsx`
- Mock data: inline constants in page; no API calls.

## Page Layout
- Header
  - Back: ghost icon button (`ArrowLeft`) id `parcego-ofd-back-btn`
  - Title: “Out for Delivery”
  - Status badge: `In Progress` or `Paused`
- Route Summary Card
  - Stats: total stops, remaining, ETA window
  - Progress bar (simple div-based)
  - Actions: `Pause`, `Resume`, `Refresh`
- Stops List
  - Each stop item shows sequence number, recipient, address, ETA badge, status chip
  - Item actions: `Navigate` (maps deeplink), `Call`, `Message`, `Scan`
  - Clicking item selects it as current stop (highlights row)
- Current Stop Card
  - Recipient details, phone, instructions
  - Map placeholder (static image or empty card with `MapPin` icon)
  - CTAs:
    - Primary: `Attempt Delivery`
    - Secondary: `Pre-drop Scan`
- Attempt Delivery Flow (UI only)
  - Dialog: select “Delivered” or “Failed”
  - Delivered sub-flow:
    - Photo capture placeholder + optional signature checkbox
    - Button: `Confirm Delivery` → show success toast
  - Failed sub-flow:
    - Reason radio list (No answer, Incorrect address, Access blocked, Other)
    - Optional notes + photo placeholder
    - Button: `Record Failed Attempt` → show warning toast
- Bottom Sticky Bar
  - Left: current stop index/remaining
  - Right actions: `Navigate`, `Call`, `Attempt Delivery`
- Offline Banner
  - Appears at top when offline; explains queued actions; `Retry` button

## Interactions & State (mocked)
- Mock stops array with fields:
  - `id`, `sequence`, `name`, `address`, `eta`, `status: "pending"|"en_route"|"delivered"|"failed"`, `phone`, `notes`
- Selected stop via local state; clicking list item updates selection and scrolls into view.
- “Attempt Delivery” opens a modal with delivered/failed tabs.
- On “Confirm Delivery”: set stop.status to `delivered`, show toast, advance to next pending stop.
- On “Record Failed Attempt”: set stop.status to `failed`, show toast, keep selection.
- “Pre-drop Scan”: opens lightweight dialog with input or mock scanner placeholder; on success, show toast.
- Offline banner toggled by a boolean; queued actions show a static count.

## IDs (examples)
- Header: `parcego-ofd-header`
- Route summary: `parcego-ofd-summary-card`
- Stops list: `parcego-ofd-stops-list`
- Stop item: `parcego-ofd-stop-item-{id}`
- Current stop card: `parcego-ofd-current-card`
- Attempt modal: `parcego-ofd-attempt-dialog`
- Delivered confirm: `parcego-ofd-delivered-confirm-btn`
- Failed confirm: `parcego-ofd-failed-confirm-btn`
- Sticky bar: `parcego-ofd-stickybar`
- Offline banner: `parcego-ofd-offline-banner`

## Accessibility
- List items are buttons with `role="button"`, `tabIndex=0`, `aria-pressed` when selected.
- Dialogs use proper roles: `role="dialog" aria-modal="true"`; focus trap and escape close.
- Buttons have `aria-label` as needed; toasts `aria-live="polite"`.

## Visual/Styling
- Minimal, high-contrast, readable sizes.
- Use `Badge` for statuses:
  - delivered: `bg-green-100 text-green-800`
  - failed: `bg-red-100 text-red-800`
  - en_route: `bg-blue-100 text-blue-800`
  - pending: `bg-gray-100 text-gray-800`
- Hover/active: light shadow and 98% scale; transitions 200–250ms.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Renders route summary, stops list, and current stop sections without API.
- Selecting a stop highlights it and updates current stop card.
- Delivered/Failed flows update the list pill badges immediately.
- Pre-drop scan dialog opens and shows success toast on mock submit.
- Sticky bar visible on mobile and desktop; responsive layout:
  - Mobile: list collapses under current card; sticky bar always visible.
  - Desktop: two-column layout (list left, current card right).
- All IDs follow `parcego-...` pattern; no duplicate IDs.
- No CLS; animations use transform/opacity only.

## Suggested Component Skeletons (TypeScript)
- Page exports default `OutForDeliveryPage` at `app/courier/out-for-delivery/page.tsx`.
- Keep components small and composable; no TODOs or dead code.
- Use `Icon` component names already present (e.g., `MapPin`, `Phone`, `Navigation`, `Camera`, `CheckCircle`, `AlertCircle`).

## Notes
- Do not integrate maps SDKs; use placeholders.
- Phone actions are UI-only; use `href="tel:..."` when needed but keep within UI-only constraints.
- Ensure reduced-motion users get instant state changes without animation.